msgid "TBS Crossfire Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:7
#: b1934bb2d9bc4c67a92ec3790213f8ad
msgid "ELRS (ExpressLRS) RC systems use the CRSF protocol and are connected in a similar manner. ELRS receivers can also be used in Mavlink mode to provide both bidirectional Mavlink telemetry and RC control over a single TX-RX pair. Details `here <https://www.expresslrs.org/software/mavlink/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:9
#: 2b410ae01794435aaf85353139557779
msgid "TBS Crossfire Receivers incorporate telemetry along with RC control information in their interface to ArduPilot. ArduPilot supports native CRSF telemetry and extensions to it that allow using the :Ref:`common-frsky-yaapu`. See :ref:`common-tbs-rc` for connection and setup information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:11
#: 8b765abd2520446bba7d08e067b87e9a
msgid "OpenTx will discover the native CRSF Telemetry sensors (but a limited number, use passthru option below for more displayed information using Yaapu Telemetry script), which then can be displayed on `OpenTX <https://www.open-tx.org/>`_ telemetry screens or repeated from the CRSF TX module's WIFI to MAVLink Ground Control Stations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:15
#: 9fe0227700c34b3fb197a87abcc73d39
msgid "These values can be displayed on OpenTX transmitters in several ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:17
#: d88599dfe9e840e1b13397db2184ce79
msgid "Using the built-in telemetry screens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:21
#: f2737e2548ee45c79bb1a8ffe80b17df
msgid "In addition, by setting :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` bit 8, additional ArduPilot telemetry items are transferred which allows use of the :ref:`common-frsky-yaapu` on OpenTX transmitters. Limitations and additional information is shown `here <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/passthrough-telemetry-over-crsf-crossfire>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:26
#: cb3a04966a1c4525bc19e2cf97bbf6e3
msgid "when using :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` bit 8 for passthru, be sure no SERIAL port is setup to use ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 10 (Passthrough) to avoid a conflict and unreliable operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:28
#: b5853adedbae4ef383b6ff67fd19ad71
msgid "Several OpenTX scripts are normally provided for adjusting CRSF TX and RX system parameters. They are accessed by long pressing the SYS button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:31
#: 79082c63235a4a7885b2762128cf4f1b
msgid "ArduPilot Parameter Editor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:33
#: 4b5609ce86784080953390dbd8106a55
msgid "In  addition, the ArduPilot CRSF implementation provides for ArduPilot parameter adjustment, similar in function to ArduPilot's :ref:`common-paramosd` feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:35
#: b54d2542a1b14447be1b3408210e35e0
msgid "If the autopilot has any active OSD (:ref:`OSD_TYPE<OSD_TYPE>` not equal to \"0\") , this feature is automatically enabled. If not, then selecting :ref:`OSD_TYPE<OSD_TYPE>` = 4 (TX only) will enable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:37
#: 81f0d9db5a3a4afca7dd137cb8359c45
msgid "Selecting the Crossfire Configuration LUA script in the transmitter will show:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:41
#: 2bee439a88534aeabe3a18aeefb87a38
msgid "And selecting the ArduPilot vehicle shown in that list will activate the :ref:`common-paramosd` with a list of all parameters which have been setup for both OSD screens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:45
#: 1dde28fa5055447e93d91ecc07c21731
msgid "Some autopilots will not display the parameter values that have text names, as text, but rather as a number, in order to save flash space. See  :ref:`common-limited_firmware` for those without CRSF TEXT capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:48
#: 1977986abb8d43bdb9dbb1f031e43d37
msgid "Scripted CRSF Menus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:50
#: 17412de78b5e49149efc06a98f908979
msgid "ArduPilot supports custom CRSF menus created via Lua scripts. These menus appear alongside the built-in ArduPilot parameter editor in the transmitter's Crossfire Configuration screen, and can be used to provide task-specific configuration interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:52
#: 6381a778ffb14c1f8cfb5cbacc1c8bd8
msgid "The `crsf_helper.lua module <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/examples/crsf-menu.lua>`__  provides a high-level API which can be placed in LUA scripts for creating CRSF menus. Multiple independent menu scripts can run simultaneously — for example, a PID tuning menu and an OSD configuration menu can coexist without conflicts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:54
#: c6b2ab9fcfcb42f3aa363380cffade94
msgid "**Multi-menu support (4.7 and later):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:56
#: 14e92a129b8c4009a0d3b9726e013882
msgid "In ArduPilot 4.7, the CRSF menu Lua API was improved to support multiple concurrent menus reliably:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:58
#: 2c2f9fe440b848cd84369564cd67f40a
msgid "New ``crsf:peek_menu_event()`` method allows scripts to inspect pending events without consuming them, so each script can check whether an event belongs to its menu before processing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:59
#: b5dfd24d003f4ee494c5e2f75c07eb5d
msgid "New ``crsf:pop_menu_event()`` method explicitly consumes an event after a script has determined it owns the event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:60
#: ca7bbd9e6e8a421299e3c9b8c0c6297d
msgid "New ``crsf:send_response()`` method for sending generic CRSF parameter responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:61
#: 46cea686bcfd4c0dae019fd85b2a34a4
msgid "Thread-safe access to the menu event queues via internal semaphore protection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-crsf-telemetry.rst:63
#: 705b6b8862834cd0b4a20add281ed6f3
msgid "Scripts using ``crsf_helper.lua`` automatically benefit from these improvements. Scripts using the low-level CRSF API directly should be updated to use the peek/pop pattern instead of the older ``crsf:get_menu_event()`` to avoid consuming events intended for other scripts."
msgstr ""
